# {{app_name}}

Lazuli app scaffolded with `lazuli new`.

## Getting started

```bash
cp .env.example .env
pnpm install                    # node deps + workspace links
pnpm setup                      # lazuli:generate + first go build (warms cache)
docker compose up -d postgres   # local database
bash scripts/bootstrap-storage.sh  # MinIO + bucket (only when @cap.File enters the app)
pnpm db:migrate                 # apply generated SQL migrations
```

Then start everything with hot reload:

```bash
pnpm dev
```

Runs api (Go via [air](https://github.com/air-verse/air)) + web (Vite HMR) concurrently. Edit any `.go`, `.tsx`, or `.ts` → reload in ~1s.

For DSL changes (`.lzi`, `.lzx`), run `pnpm lazuli:generate` manually — codegen is intentionally NOT in the watcher to avoid racing with file watchers.

## Layout

- `app/` — product kernel: app manifest, design tokens, registry, and features.
- `app/features/` — domain features (`.lzi`). Each is a Lazuli capability bundle.
- `app/features/<f>/handlers/` — user-authored Go handlers wired via `lazuli.RegisterFn(...)`.
- `app/web/` — React/Vite frontend: shell, theme, UI primitives, routes.
- `Lazurite.toml` — workspace manifest (Lazuli framework pin, plugins, codegen settings).
- `.air.toml` — Go hot-reload config (see `pnpm go:watch`).
- `dist/` — generated artifacts (regen-overwritable; do not edit hand-authored Lazuli IR there).

## Canonical sibling layout

`Lazurite.toml [lazuli] path = "../lazuli"` assumes this directory structure on disk:

```
<root>/
├── lazuli/                     # Lazuli framework source
├── dev/                        # local plugin checkouts (one repo per plugin)
│   └── lazuli-plugin-X/
└── {{app_slug}}/               # this app
```

Check out everything as siblings under one parent. `pnpm dev` and `lazuli generate` resolve paths relative to this layout.

## CI / CD (strict-by-default)

Two GitHub Actions workflows ship in `.github/workflows/`:

- **`lazuli.yml`** runs on every push and PR. Mirrors `pnpm verify:all` exactly: `check` → `doctor --security-profile strict --coverage` → `generate` + `go build` + `tsc` → `lazuli test --layer handler`. A Postgres service container provides the real DB the handler tests run against (no mocks — per CLAUDE.md). Uploads the doctor coverage report as a build artifact.
- **`release.yml`** fires on `v*.*.*` tags. Re-runs the verify chain, then hands off to a `deploy` step intentionally left as a stub — wire it to your target (Fly.io, Render, k8s, VPS, etc.).

To **soften any individual gate** while migrating off a baseline, do NOT edit the workflows — author a `[doctor.test_discipline.severity_override.<RULE>]` entry in `Lazurite.toml` with a `reason` (DOCTOR-OVERRIDE-NEEDS-REASON-001 enforces). That way the override is reviewable per-PR.

To **mirror CI locally** before pushing:

```bash
pnpm verify:all   # = doctor + generate + go build + typecheck + build + lazuli test
```

Green locally ⇒ green on CI.

## Scripts cheat sheet

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `pnpm dev` | full stack with hot reload (api + web) |
| `pnpm setup` | one-time first-run: codegen + warm go build cache |
| `pnpm build` | production build (Go binary + Vite bundle) |
| `pnpm typecheck` | TypeScript check (auto-runs codegen first) |
| `pnpm lazuli:generate` | regenerate `dist/go` + `dist/ts-web` from `.lzi`/`.lzx` |
| `pnpm lazuli:doctor` | strict-profile doctor + per-layer coverage report |
| `pnpm lazuli:doctor:gate` | narrower CI gate (fails only on TestDiscipline errors) |
| `pnpm lazuli:test` | wire-thin test runner — `go test` over every handler |
| `pnpm lazuli:test:watch` | same, watching the file tree |
| `pnpm verify:all` | full pre-merge gate (doctor + codegen + build + typecheck + tests) |
| `pnpm go:watch` | api only with hot reload |
| `pnpm stack:up` | db up + codegen + migrate + build (no run) |
| `pnpm db:migrate` | apply generated SQL migrations |
